  "Question": "Ana’s monthly salary was \\(\\$2000\\) in May. In June she received a \\(20\\%\\) raise. In July she received a \\(20\\%\\) pay cut. After the two changes in June and July, Ana’s monthly salary was",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$1920\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$1980\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$2000\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$2020\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$2040\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "July's pay cut is based on June's salary, so first find the salary after the raise. Since \\(20\\%=0.20\\), the June raise is\n\\[\n0.20\\cdot2000=400\n\\]\ndollars. June's monthly salary is therefore \\(2000+400=2400\\) dollars. The July cut is\n\\[\n0.20\\cdot2400=480\n\\]\ndollars, leaving \\(2400-480=1920\\) dollars. Thus Ana's monthly salary after both changes is \\(1920\\) dollars, choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
